    "operation_spec": {
      "definition": "catalogue.identifier-audit/1 takes a schema-conforming snapshot string, finite items array, complete boolean and fixed formal_input object and returns snapshot unchanged, count = length(items), distinct = true exactly when every unordered pair of item id strings differs under exact case-sensitive Unicode string equality, complete unchanged and typed_input = formal_input unchanged. Count includes duplicates. Empty items gives count 0 and distinct true. Do not acquire data, trim, normalise, case-fold, sort, filter, reorder or substitute identities. Reject inputs outside the fixed schema. The surrounding acquisition envelope records the actual UTC RFC3339 calculation time ending in Z and preserves the original request and context while the executor separately retains every upstream original observation time and provenance.",
      "input_conditions": [
        "The complete input satisfies the fixed input schema with no additional properties.",
        "There are at most 32 items and each item has only a nonempty id string of 1–64 characters.",
        "The snapshot string has 1–128 characters.",
        "formal_input is the exact fixed formal conjunction object rather than a measured observation.",
        "Before qualification an independent assessor freezes full expected outputs for empty, singleton, three-distinct, duplicate, a/A and complete-false fixtures and checks schema boundaries and rejection."
      ],
